control_cli_events {"model": "gpt-6-luna", "events": "{\"type\":\"thread.started\",\"thread_id\":\"01a1674b-4ba0-7d01-92f4-83107692f085\"}\n{\"type\":\"turn.started\"}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_0\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"{\\\"task_summary\\\":\\\"Extend the existing public API with prefix_many(cases: list[tuple]) -> list, preserving the day-1 API. Add unittest coverage and update HANDOFF.md with verification evidence.\\\",\\\"constraints\\\":[\\\"Keep the day-1 API compatible.\\\",\\\"Each tuple supplies positional arguments for one call to prefix; return results in case order and [] for no cases.\\\",\\\"Propagate the first exception unchanged.\\\",\\\"Do not mutate cases or arguments.\\\",\\\"Keep at least three passing unittest test methods in test_solution.py, including batch coverage.\\\",\\\"HANDOFF.md must record the verification command and its observed result.\\\",\\\"Work only in the supplied task workspace; do not access parent repositories or external services.\\\"],\\\"success_criteria\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-1\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"solution.py defines the typed public function prefix_many(cases: list[tuple]) -> list.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"regex\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"solution.py\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"def\\\\\\\\s+prefix_many\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\\(\\\\\\\\s*cases\\\\\\\\s*:\\\\\\\\s*list\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\\[\\\\\\\\s*tuple\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\\]\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\\)\\\\\\\\s*->\\\\\\\\s*list\\\\\\\\b\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-2\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"The implementation returns the results of calling prefix with each tuple's positional arguments, in case order, returns an empty list for no cases, and propagates the first exception unchanged.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"llm_judge\\\",\\\"rubric\\\":\\\"Read the workspace source files. Assess whether prefix_many calls prefix once per case using that tuple as positional arguments, returns results in input order, returns [] for no cases, and lets the first exception propagate unchanged. Assess only behavior evident from the implementation.\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-3\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"The implementation preserves the day-1 prefix API and does not mutate cases or their argument tuples or contents.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"llm_judge\\\",\\\"rubric\\\":\\\"Read the workspace source files. Assess whether the day-1 public prefix API remains compatible and whether prefix_many avoids mutating cases or supplied arguments. Base the assessment only on source code.\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-4\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"test_solution.py contains at least three unittest test methods, including batch coverage.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"regex\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"test_solution.py\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"(?s)(?=.*class\\\\\\\\s+\\\\\\\\w+\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\\(\\\\\\\\s*unittest\\\\\\\\.TestCase\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\\))(?=(?:.*?def\\\\\\\\s+test_){3,})(?=.*def\\\\\\\\s+test_\\\\\\\\w*.*(?:batch|many|cases))\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-5\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"The unittest suite completes successfully.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"command\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -m unittest discover -v\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-6\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"HANDOFF.md records the verification command and its observed result.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"regex\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"HANDOFF.md\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"(?s)(?=.*python -m unittest discover -v)(?=.*(?:passed|OK|successfully|successful))\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"SC-7\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"solution.py and test_solution.py compile as Python modules.\\\",\\\"check\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"command\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -m py_compile solution.py test_solution.py\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}}}],\\\"verification\\\":[{\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -m unittest discover -v\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}},{\\\"command\\\":\\\"python -m py_compile solution.py test_solution.py\\\",\\\"expected\\\":{\\\"exit_code\\\":0}}],\\\"stop_conditions\\\":[],\\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"The handoff's named files solution.py, test_solution.py, and HANDOFF.md are relative paths in the supplied workspace.\\\",\\\"The file solution.py may not exist yet and may be created as needed; the same applies to test_solution.py and HANDOFF.md if absent.\\\",\\\"The user-requested observed verification result in HANDOFF.md is to be recorded after running the unittest command; the proposed check only assesses whether the command and a success result are documented.\\\",\\\"The runner-provided handoff accurately describes the day-1 API and its existing behavior; those claims remain subject to review in the workspace.\\\",\\\"The function annotation list[tuple] is interpreted literally as requested, without specifying tuple element types.\\\"]}\"}}\n{\"type\":\"turn.completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":17669,\"cached_input_tokens\":14976,\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":867,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":0}}\n"}
